  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "A Muslim first name and a family name from the father, fixed by the civil registry in the 1900s. Family names often start with El, Ben or Bel, or name a place or trade: El Fassi (from Fez), Tazi (from Taza), Haddad (smith). Old Fez families carry names like Bennani, Berrada and Benjelloun. Amazigh families, many of them from the Souss, carry names like Ait Lahcen or Ouhammou, where Ait means 'the people of' and Ou means 'son of', and give Amazigh first names like Itto, Tiziri, Yuba and Anir. Fatima Zahra and Mohamed Amine style double names are very common.",
